        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "612da4ce-d335-534d-bb0d-99271c1dca1b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Naomi Watts, Scott Coffey\n- Works: Ellie Parker, For Love Alone, Hey Dad..!, Built Like Alaska's third album\n- Organizations: Built Like Alaska\n- Places: Los Angeles, Oakdale, Modesto, the U.S.\n- Topics: film scoring, acting careers, touring\n\nFacts:\n- Naomi Watts was born on 28 September 1968 and is an English actress and film producer.\n- Naomi Watts made her screen debut in the Australian drama film \"For Love Alone\" in 1986.\n- Naomi Watts then appeared in the Australian television series \"Hey Dad..!\".\n- In 2005, \"Ellie Parker\" was released as an American drama-comedy film written and directed by Scott Coffey.\n- In 2005, Naomi Watts played the title character in \"Ellie Parker,\" a young woman struggling as an actress in Los Angeles.\n- Also in 2005, Built Like Alaska provided the score for Scott Coffey's film \"Ellie Parker\" and spent much of the summer touring the U.S.\n- Built Like Alaska later completed work on an untitled third album that the band recorded in Oakdale and that Lucky Lew mixed at Wave Parade in Modesto.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
